---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import DownloadLink from '../components/DownloadLink.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { featuredQuestions } from '../data/faq';
import { APP_ARCHIVER_URL, DEVELOPER_URL, BLOG_URL, MORE_APPS_URL } from '../consts';
import overview from '../assets/diskpress-overview.png';
import menuBar from '../assets/diskpress-menu-bar.png';
import oneTimeReview from '../assets/diskpress-one-time-review.png';
import oneTimeResults from '../assets/diskpress-one-time-results.png';
import locations from '../assets/diskpress-locations.png';
import exclusions from '../assets/diskpress-exclusions.png';

const detailScreenshotSizes = '(max-width: 600px) calc(100vw - 98px), (max-width: 780px) calc(92vw - 50px), (max-width: 1440px) calc(46vw - 62px), 600px';
---
<SiteLayout>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Native storage optimization for Mac</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading">More room.<br /><span>Same files.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Save space without deleting what you want to keep. DiskPress combines native file compression and file deduplication. Your files stay in place and open normally.</p>
      <div class="hero-download"><DownloadLink /><p class="fine">macOS 10.15 or later. Built for APFS. Works offline.</p></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">Meet your new space saver</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-visual">
      <Image src={overview} alt="DiskPress Overview in light appearance showing disk space, compression and deduplication savings, recent savings, and enabled background monitoring." widths={[480, 768, 1024, 1440, 1622]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) 90vw, (max-width: 1440px) 55vw, 760px" format="webp" quality={90} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption>DiskPress Overview with example data. Your savings will vary.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="benefits">
      <div class="benefit"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h2>Your files stay yours</h2><p>Lossless storage. Same contents and paths.</p></div></div>
      <div class="benefit"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h2>Keep the savings. Quit the app.</h2><p>macOS reads optimized files on its own.</p></div></div>
      <div class="benefit"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><h2>Entirely on your Mac</h2><p>No uploads, analytics, or telemetry in the app.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section comparison-section" id="why-diskpress">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A different way to make room</p><h2>You need more space.<br />Not fewer things.</h2><p class="lead">Cleaning has its place. But deleting useful files is a compromise, and cleared caches can quickly grow back. DiskPress gives you another option.</p></div>
      <div class="comparison-grid">
        <div class="comparison-item"><span class="comparison-label">Remove apps and files</span><h3>Space from deletion</h3><p>A cleaner can help find things you no longer need. To get the space back, you have to let those things go.</p><p class="comparison-result">Useful when you want less stuff.</p></div>
        <div class="comparison-item"><span class="comparison-label">Clear caches</span><h3>Space for the moment</h3><p>Removing temporary data can free space now. As you keep using your apps, many caches are created again.</p><p class="comparison-result">Useful for a temporary cleanup.</p></div>
        <div class="comparison-item featured"><span class="comparison-label">Optimize with DiskPress</span><h3>Space without deleting</h3><p>File compression and file deduplication work together to save space. Keep supported files right where they are, without deleting duplicate copies.</p><p class="comparison-result">Made for what you want to keep.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Built into your Mac. Put to work.</p><h2>Two techniques.<br />Working together.</h2><p class="lead">DiskPress combines file compression and file deduplication in one optimization workflow. Compressible files use fewer bytes, and identical files can share those bytes for even more savings. No archive format. No special reader.</p></div>
    <div class="native-grid">
      <article class="native-feature"><span class="feature-number">01</span><h3>File compression</h3><p>Lossless native compression stores supported files using fewer bytes. macOS decompresses them as they are read, without changing their contents or making you unpack anything.</p><p class="feature-note">Best for compressible, uncompressed user data.</p></article>
      <article class="native-feature"><span class="feature-number">02</span><h3>File deduplication</h3><p>When entire files match, DiskPress verifies their contents and uses APFS clones to share storage, including compressed data. Each file stays independent. Editing one does not change the others.</p><p class="feature-note">Identical files on the same compatible volume.</p></article>
    </div>
    <figure class="savings-example" id="combined-savings" aria-labelledby="savings-example-heading">
      <figcaption class="savings-example-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">An illustrative example</p>
        <h3 id="savings-example-heading">Two files. 65% less storage.</h3>
        <p>Start with two identical, uncompressed 100 MB files stored separately on the same compatible APFS volume. Suppose file compression reduces their data by 30%.</p>
      </figcaption>
      <ol class="savings-stages" role="list" aria-label="Total physical data storage in this example">
        <li data-savings-stage="original">
          <span class="savings-stage-label">Before optimization</span>
          <strong class="savings-value">200 MB</strong>
          <div class="savings-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: 100%"></span></div>
          <p>100 MB + 100 MB, stored separately.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-savings-stage="compressed">
          <span class="savings-stage-label">After compression</span>
          <strong class="savings-value">140 MB</strong>
          <div class="savings-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: 70%"></span></div>
          <p>70 MB + 70 MB after 30% compression.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-savings-stage="combined">
          <span class="savings-stage-label">After both techniques</span>
          <strong class="savings-value">70 MB</strong>
          <div class="savings-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width: 35%"></span></div>
          <p>File deduplication adds to the savings by sharing the same 70 MB of compressed data.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="savings-example-result">
        <p><strong>130 MB saved.</strong> Both files stay in place and open normally.</p>
        <p class="savings-equation">130 MB out of 200 MB = <strong>65% saved</strong></p>
      </div>
      <p class="savings-example-note">Illustrative data sizes, not a benchmark or a guarantee. Actual savings vary with your files, settings, and filesystem overhead. Snapshots can delay an increase in free space. <a href="/faq/#combined-savings">Understand combined savings</a>.</p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="your-workflow">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">One folder or your everyday routine</p><h2>Your files.<br />Your workflow.</h2><p class="lead">Optimize a selection now, or choose mostly stable folders to keep efficient over time.</p><a class="text-link" href="/faq/#one-time">Find your workflow</a></div>
        <div class="workflow-steps">
          <article><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h3>Drop it. Optimize it.</h3><p>Drag files or folders into DiskPress. Pin it to your Dock and drop them onto the app icon for one-time optimization, without adding a monitored location.</p></div></article>
          <article><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h3>Choose the folders you keep</h3><p>Save specific locations with files you keep and change infrequently. Review their storage, then use Optimize Now when ready. Adding a location does not immediately optimize it.</p></div></article>
          <article><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h3>Let the background do the work</h3><p>Enable automatic monitoring to revisit your enabled locations on a schedule. Recent-file protection gives newly changed files time to settle.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="safety-note"><strong>Save space thoughtfully.</strong> Optimization rewrites files at their existing paths and can add disk writes. Exclude locations with frequent new or changing files to avoid unnecessary SSD wear. For active work, wait until the files settle and optimize once. <a href="/faq/#ssd-wear">Learn how to choose suitable folders</a>.</p>
      <div class="screenshot-grid">
        <figure class="screenshot-figure">
          <figcaption><h3>Review before you optimize</h3><p>Check the selected location, file count, and existing savings before starting.</p></figcaption>
          <Image src={oneTimeReview} alt="DiskPress one-time optimization review showing the selected Design Project folder, file count, actual size, and the Optimize button." widths={[480, 768, 1024, 1280]} sizes={detailScreenshotSizes} format="webp" quality={90} loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-figure">
          <figcaption><h3>See the finished result</h3><p>Review combined savings, file compression and file deduplication results, and any skipped files.</p></figcaption>
          <Image src={oneTimeResults} alt="DiskPress one-time optimization results showing estimated space saved, sizes before and after, and counts of compressed and deduplicated files." widths={[480, 768, 1024, 1280]} sizes={detailScreenshotSizes} format="webp" quality={90} loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="screenshot-disclaimer">App screenshots use example data. Savings depend on your files and settings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap menu-section" id="background">
    <div class="menu-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Small presence. Useful perspective.</p><h2>Quietly working.<br />Always within reach.</h2><p class="lead">Keep DiskPress in the menu bar while monitoring is on. Check its progress, see your savings, and get back to what you were doing.</p>
      <div class="detail-list">
        <div><h3>Your storage at a glance</h3><p>See available space, current measured savings, and savings from the last 24 hours, 7 days, and 30 days.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The right controls, one click away</h3><p>Add a location, optimize now, open Settings, or stop monitoring directly from the menu.</p></div>
        <div><h3>A pace that fits your Mac</h3><p>Choose Low CPU, Balanced, Fast, or Fastest. Set separate power and battery profiles, or pause automatic work on battery.</p></div>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/faq/#login-and-quit">How background mode and login work</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="menu-visual"><Image src={menuBar} alt="DiskPress menu bar panel in light appearance showing the next scheduled scan, disk space and savings, with Open DiskPress, Add Location, Optimize Now, Stop Monitoring, Settings, and Quit actions." widths={[360, 540, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) 85vw, 390px" format="webp" quality={90} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Menu bar controls are available while monitoring is on.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section automation-section" id="automation">
    <div class="wrap automation-grid">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">For scripts, workflows, and AI agents</p><h2>A full CLI.<br />No open window required.</h2><p class="lead">Inspect targets, optimize files, and read settings, activity, and savings with structured JSON output. The command line uses the same local engine as the app.</p><p>Authorize your folders once in Settings. Then run commands without opening the main window or turning on recurring monitoring.</p><a class="text-link" href="/cli/">Read the CLI guide</a></div>
      <div class="automation-example"><CodeBlock id="home-cli" label="Start with the built-in help" code={'"/Applications/DiskPress.app/Contents/MacOS/DiskPress" --help'} /><div class="command-list"><div><code>scan</code><span>Inspect eligibility without optimizing</span></div><div><code>optimize</code><span>Compress and deduplicate selected targets</span></div><div><code>overview</code><span>Read storage and savings information</span></div><div><code>--json</code><span>Get structured events for automation</span></div></div><p class="fine">DiskPress stays offline. Your chosen AI agent has its own data-sharing practices.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="in-control">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Deliberate about your data</p><h2>Useful automation.<br />Clear boundaries.</h2></div>
    <div class="control-grid">
      <article><h3>Choose what is included</h3><p>Control locations, file-size limits, minimum savings, hidden files, and editable exclusion rules. Common compressed media and archive formats are excluded by default.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Know what happened</h3><p>Watch progress, cancel safely, and review per-file results in Activity. Rescan your saved locations to refresh current savings. Completed work stays optimized after cancellation.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep it on your Mac</h3><p>No account. No uploads. No app analytics or telemetry. Verification and recovery happen locally, along with the optimization itself.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy-policy/">Read the privacy policy</a></article>
    </div>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <figure class="screenshot-figure">
        <figcaption><h3>Keep your locations organized</h3><p>Review saved folders and their measured savings. Enable only the locations that suit your workflow.</p></figcaption>
        <Image src={locations} alt="DiskPress Locations listing example folders with their enabled status, total size, and measured savings, plus Add, Remove, Disable, and Optimize Now controls." widths={[480, 768, 1024, 1440, 1622]} sizes={detailScreenshotSizes} format="webp" quality={90} loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <figure class="screenshot-figure">
        <figcaption><h3>Decide what to leave alone</h3><p>Use exclusion rules to skip unsuitable files, including common compressed media and archive formats.</p></figcaption>
        <Image src={exclusions} alt="DiskPress Settings with the Exclusions tab selected, showing enabled file groups for archives, disk images, installers, images, audio, and video." widths={[480, 768, 1024, 1440, 1622]} sizes={detailScreenshotSizes} format="webp" quality={90} loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="safety-note">DiskPress changes how files are stored. Keep an independent backup of important data. System locations, application bundles, executables, and other unsupported targets are intentionally skipped. <a href="/faq/#verification-backup">Read about safeguards and limits</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap companion-section" aria-labelledby="companion-heading"><div class="companion-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">The right tool for each job</p><h2 id="companion-heading">DiskPress for your files.<br />App Archiver for your apps.</h2></div><div><p>DiskPress does not compress application bundles or executables. Optimizing installed software needs a more specialized architecture.</p><p>App Archiver is <a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a>'s dedicated app for compressing, optimizing, and archiving supported Mac apps. Together, the two tools cover different parts of what you keep.</p><a class="text-link" href={APP_ARCHIVER_URL}>Discover App Archiver</a></div></div></section>

  <section class="section wrap maker-section" id="developer">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A note from the developer</p><h2>I wanted the space.<br />I still wanted my files.</h2></div>
    <div class="maker-story"><p>"I built DiskPress because deleting things is not always the answer. My Mac already had the filesystem features to store files more efficiently. What I wanted was a simple way to choose my folders and let those features keep working in the background."</p><p>"DiskPress is my way of making that routine. Keep the files you need, make better use of the SSD you already have, and stay in control of the work."</p><div class="maker-signature"><strong><a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a></strong><span>Developer of DiskPress and other focused Mac utilities</span></div><div class="maker-links"><a class="text-link" href={MORE_APPS_URL}>Explore my other apps</a><a class="text-link" href={BLOG_URL}>Read Reverse Everything</a></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section"><div class="wrap home-faq-grid"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Good questions</p><h2>A few things<br />worth knowing.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">Explore the full FAQ</a></div><FaqList questions={featuredQuestions} /></div></section>

  <section class="section wrap closing-section"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="64" height="64" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h2>Make room for<br />what comes next.</h2><p class="lead">Start with a folder. Keep what matters.</p><DownloadLink /><p class="fine">macOS 10.15 or later. Results vary by file and filesystem.</p></section>
</SiteLayout>
